From: tabby-machine-user-514235 <tabby-machine-user-514235@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 16:09:31 -0300
Subject: fix: deliver position override to pending geolocation queries

GeolocationImpl::SetOverride flushes a pending QueryNextPosition callback
before installing the new override. current_result_ is always null at that
point (it is moved out whenever a position is reported), so the flush
synthesizes a POSITION_UNAVAILABLE error. With an open watchPosition the
frame always has a pending query, so every re-applied
Emulation.setGeolocationOverride surfaces a spurious error-code-2 to the
page, killing any getCurrentPosition({maximumAge: 0}) waiting on the same
frame's shared mojo pipe.

Flush with the incoming override result instead: the pending query receives
the position (or the intentional error override) directly, and re-applying
the override on an interval behaves like a real location provider. When the
flush delivered the result, the trailing OnLocationUpdate is skipped so the
client's re-armed query does not consume a cached copy of the same result
and observe it twice (identical timestamp, ~1ms apart) per application;
when there was no pending query (e.g. at BindGeolocation time) the result
is cached exactly as before.

This is a general Chromium bug, not an Electron-specific change; it should
be upstreamed. The patch can be dropped once upstream
services/device/geolocation/geolocation_impl.cc no longer synthesizes
kPositionUnavailable in SetOverride when current_result_ is null.

diff --git a/services/device/geolocation/geolocation_impl.cc b/services/device/geolocation/geolocation_impl.cc
index bf60741c22d58f6f0a97e892447ecfd9465a058d..110f1f67970c8d014f18c6cbcf8c9920d31831d9 100644
--- a/services/device/geolocation/geolocation_impl.cc
+++ b/services/device/geolocation/geolocation_impl.cc
@@ -140,12 +140,14 @@ void GeolocationImpl::QueryCachedPosition(
 }
 
 void GeolocationImpl::SetOverride(const mojom::GeopositionResult& result) {
+  bool flushed_incoming_result = false;
   if (!position_callback_.is_null()) {
     if (!current_result_) {
-      current_result_ =
-          mojom::GeopositionResult::NewError(mojom::GeopositionError::New(
-              mojom::GeopositionErrorCode::kPositionUnavailable,
-              /*error_message=*/"", /*error_technical=*/""));
+      // Flush the pending query with the incoming override instead of a
+      // synthesized POSITION_UNAVAILABLE, so re-applying a position override
+      // never surfaces a spurious error to a waiting watcher or one-shot.
+      current_result_ = result.Clone();
+      flushed_incoming_result = true;
     }
     ReportCurrentPosition();
   }
@@ -158,7 +160,12 @@ void GeolocationImpl::SetOverride(const mojom::GeopositionResult& result) {
 
   geolocation_subscription_ = {};
 
-  OnLocationUpdate(*position_override_);
+  // When the flush above already delivered this result, don't also cache it:
+  // the client's re-armed query would consume the cached copy and observe the
+  // same position twice (same timestamp, ~1ms apart) per override application.
+  if (!flushed_incoming_result) {
+    OnLocationUpdate(*position_override_);
+  }
 }
 
 void GeolocationImpl::ClearOverride() {
